    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Acceptance of terms</h2>
    <p style="font-size:16px;color:#39414B;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:20px">By using this website or engaging Writ Large for document-preparation services, you agree to these Terms of Service. If you do not agree, please do not use this website or our services.</p>

    <h2>Description of services</h2>
    <p style="font-size:16px;color:#39414B;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:20px">Writ Large is a paralegal document-preparation service for federal post-conviction matters, including motions under 28 U.S.C. § 2255, habeas corpus petitions under 28 U.S.C. § 2241, compassionate release motions under 18 U.S.C. § 3582(c)(1)(A), First Step Act time-credit claims, and immigration § 2241 matters. We also offer document retrieval and organization through the Case File service, and a free transfer-request tool. Writ Large is not a law firm, does not currently employ attorneys directly, and does not provide individualized legal advice.</p>

    <h2>No attorney-client relationship</h2>
    <p style="font-size:16px;color:#39414B;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:20px">Using this website, submitting a form, purchasing a service, or communicating with Writ Large does not create an attorney-client relationship or attorney-client privilege. Our writing team consists of trained paralegals with experience in the federal post-conviction system, working under the oversight of a licensed attorney. We prepare documents for you to review, sign, and file yourself, unless a separate written agreement says otherwise.</p>

    <h2>What our services are — and are not</h2>
    <p style="font-size:16px;color:#39414B;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:20px">Document preparation means we draft the motion, petition, or filing based on the facts and records you provide. The Case File service means we retrieve what is publicly filed in your case and organize it — we do not evaluate the case, recommend a course of action, or tell you what to file. In every service, you remain responsible for reviewing every document for accuracy before signing, for filing it yourself with the court, and for every deadline that applies to your matter.</p>

    <h2>No guarantee of results</h2>
    <p style="font-size:16px;color:#39414B;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:20px">No outcome, timeline, or result is guaranteed. Courts — not Writ Large — decide the outcome of any filing. Prior results, where referenced, do not guarantee a similar outcome in any other matter.</p>

    <h2>Payment, pricing, and engagement</h2>
    <p style="font-size:16px;color:#39414B;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:20px">Pricing for the Case File service is flat and shown on our <a href="/pricing/">Pricing</a> page. Pricing for document-preparation services is quoted individually once we understand what your case requires, and may be offered as a single payment or as a monthly payment plan. Payment is processed securely through Stripe; we never see or store your card details. Work on your matter begins after payment, or after the first installment on a payment plan, unless we agree otherwise in writing.</p>

    <h2>Cancellations and refunds</h2>
    <p style="font-size:16px;color:#39414B;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:20px">See our <a href="/refund-policy/">Refund Policy</a> for the specific terms governing cancellations, refunds, and monthly payment plans. It is part of these Terms.</p>

    <h2>Your responsibilities</h2>
    <p style="font-size:16px;color:#39414B;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:20px">You are responsible for the accuracy and completeness of the information and records you provide to us. Delays or errors caused by incomplete or inaccurate information are not the responsibility of Writ Large. You remain responsible for all filing deadlines and procedural requirements applicable to your matter at all times.</p>

    <h2>Website content</h2>
    <p style="font-size:16px;color:#39414B;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:20px">Articles, videos, and other content on this website are provided for general educational purposes only and do not constitute legal advice for any specific situation. Legal advice can only be provided by a licensed attorney with knowledge of the specific facts of your matter.</p>

    <h2>Monitored communications</h2>
    <p style="font-size:16px;color:#39414B;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:20px">Telephone calls and electronic messages from correctional facilities may be monitored or recorded by the facility. Consider that before discussing sensitive details through a monitored channel.</p>

    <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
    <p style="font-size:16px;color:#39414B;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:20px">The content, design, and organization of this website are the property of Writ Large, a service of Prisoner Legal Aid LLC, and may not be copied or reproduced without permission, except as permitted by applicable law.</p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p style="font-size:16px;color:#39414B;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:20px">This website and its content are provided "as is," without warranties of any kind. Writ Large is not liable for any decisions made in reliance on general educational content provided on this website.</p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
